Broward County Sheriff Scott Israel  faces new calls to resign after claims  that more than one of his deputies  failed to confront the gunman at Marjory  Stoneman Douglas high school students  and parents returned to the campus  yesterday for the first time since the  shooting Manuel Bojorquez is outside  Stoneman Douglas high in parkland  Florida where classes resumed on  Wednesday and well good morning good  morning sources tell our Miami station  WFOR that his Coral Springs police  officers responded to the shooting they  say they found multiple Broward County  sheriff's deputies waiting outside the  school meanwhile teachers and counselors  met with students here yesterday as they  prepare to head back to class flowers  and letters filled a memorial along the  sidewalk outside campus on Sunday for  many students the emotion is still raw  it hurts I broke its heart  17 people dressed as angels one for each  person killed gathered nearby walking  into the school I feel empowered to see  all this love as students prepare to  return to class the Broward County  Sheriff's Office is facing mounting  pressure over its response to the  shooting including at least one deputy  who resigned after failing to enter the  building during the rampage Broward  County Sheriff Scott Israel on Sunday  said he has displayed amazing leadership  deputies make mistakes police officers  make mistakes we all make mistakes  Israel says his office is looking into  claims at at least three other deputies  failed to confront the alleged gunman  during the shooting the department is  also accused of mishandling some of the  18 phone tips involving the suspected  shooter 16 of them we believe were  handled exactly the way they should two  of them we're not sure if our deputies  did everything they could ever should  have more than 70 Republican state  lawmakers on Sunday demanded Florida  Governor Rick Scott suspend Israel the  same day Scott announced a state run  investigation into the law enforcement  response to the shooting who was called  what was their process how was it broken  give us the facts  according to an internal investigation  sheriff Israel insists that only one of  his deputies was present on campus while  the gunman was there his office says it  will cooperate with the state's  investigation and sheriff Israel says he  will not resign John then well thanks
 

